# Cloudflare Pages redirects (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/)
#
# Posts live at the root: blog.akibh.dev/<slug>/ (plan24). Every older URL
# shape for a post 301s there — 301 = permanent, so search engines move
# the ranking. One placeholder rule per shape covers every post because the
# folder name IS the slug (content.config.ts generateId); a post that
# overrides `slug:` falls through to the 404, whose "did you mean" matcher
# still suggests it.
#   /posts/<slug>/              the blog's first URL scheme (plan19)
#   /content/<year>/<slug>/     the notes repo's Jekyll/GitHub Pages layout
/posts/:slug/                /:slug/  301
/posts/:slug                 /:slug/  301
/content/:year/:slug/        /:slug/  301
/content/:year/:slug         /:slug/  301
/notes/content/:year/:slug/  /:slug/  301
/notes/content/:year/:slug   /:slug/  301

# The tags index and search are home-page sections (plan23).
/tags/   /#tags    301
/tags    /#tags    301
/search/ /#search  301
/search  /#search  301
